\description{
\ifelse{html}{\href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#experimental}{\figure{lifecycle-experimental.svg}{options: alt='[Experimental]'}}}{\strong{[Experimental]}}

\code{wjp_cards()} draws a grid of rounded cards, one per row and column
combination, colored on a sequential scale by their value, with the value
printed in each card and, optionally, its difference from a reference card
printed below it. Rows are labeled at the left and columns at the top.
}
\details{
The function expects one row per card: the row label in \code{rows}, the column
label in \code{cols}, and the value in \code{target}. Rows and columns are drawn in
order of first appearance, or in the order given by \code{row_order} and
\code{col_order}.

\strong{Reference and differences.} With \code{ref = "row"}, the cards of the
first row are the references of their columns; with \code{ref = "col"}, the cards
of the first column are the references of their rows. Reference cards show
their value centered; the other cards show the value and, below it, the
difference from their reference: the \code{deltas} column as given or, when
\code{deltas} is \code{NULL}, the difference between the rounded values in
percentage points (e.g., \code{"+16 points"}). \code{ref = "none"} draws values only.
A card with an empty or missing delta also shows its value centered.

\strong{Colors.} The fill of each card mixes \code{colors[1]} and \code{colors[2]} in
RGB space (see \code{\link[=scale_fill_wjp_seq]{scale_fill_wjp_seq()}}) at
\code{min_shade + (1 - min_shade) * (value - limits[1]) / diff(limits)}. With
\code{label_color = "auto"}, texts on cards past \code{dark_threshold} are white.

\strong{Geometry in points.} Cards are \code{card_height} points high,
\code{card_width} points wide (or as wide as a figure of \code{width} points allows),
and \code{card_gap} points apart, with corners of \code{radius} points. Row labels are
wrapped to \code{label_width - 4} points and right-aligned \code{label_gap} points
before the cards; column headers are wrapped to the card width minus 8
points and their last line sits \code{header_gap} points above the cards. The
chart has a definite size, so \code{\link[=wjp_save]{wjp_save()}} needs no \code{width} or \code{height}.
Text widths are measured with \pkg{systemfonts} when it knows the font
family (see \code{\link[=wjp_fonts]{wjp_fonts()}}), and estimated otherwise.
}
